		<title>By: Sarah Eckrich</title>
		<link>http://fffff.at/available-online-for-free-the-sticker/comment-page-2/#comment-13962</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Sarah Eckrich]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 28 Jul 2010 18:06:49 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://fffff.at/?p=1178#comment-13962</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[As someone who has worked for minimum wage scraping, sweeping, and cleaning up after careless others, I can honestly say this does nothing to offend me. So what if someone has to peal it off? That&#039;s what you&#039;re hired to do. Suck it up and quit complaining. If you disagree with the sentiment, fine. But since when is removing a sticker the size of a small fist some big physical chore? I mean is it REALLY going to hinder anyone that much? Grow up.
That being said, I think this is fantastic. Us minimum wagers are well aware of the ridiculous costs of buying anything anymore from greedy corporations who only spend a fraction of the price developing, producing and marketing their products. (You would think others slaving away to make nothing would identify with this, by the way, and not criticize it. Pick a side and stick to it you pseudo intellectual pussies. Maybe if you did stuff with your free time that wasn&#039;t criticizing people online, you could find a job making more than minimum wage...)]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>As someone who has worked for minimum wage scraping, sweeping, and cleaning up after careless others, I can honestly say this does nothing to offend me. So what if someone has to peal it off? That&#8217;s what you&#8217;re hired to do. Suck it up and quit complaining. If you disagree with the sentiment, fine. But since when is removing a sticker the size of a small fist some big physical chore? I mean is it REALLY going to hinder anyone that much? Grow up.<br />
That being said, I think this is fantastic. Us minimum wagers are well aware of the ridiculous costs of buying anything anymore from greedy corporations who only spend a fraction of the price developing, producing and marketing their products. (You would think others slaving away to make nothing would identify with this, by the way, and not criticize it. Pick a side and stick to it you pseudo intellectual pussies. Maybe if you did stuff with your free time that wasn&#8217;t criticizing people online, you could find a job making more than minimum wage&#8230;)</p>
]]></content:encoded>
